    {
      "slug": "fake-customer-costume",
      "script": "Wrong employee—twice? I was comparing two blenders in the kitchen aisle when a woman marched over holding a cracked air fryer and ordered me to fix it. I told her I didn't work there. My blue jacket proved otherwise. I pointed to my charity fun run shirt and the actual employee vest hanging two feet away. She ignored both, flagged down a real manager, and accused me of hiding behind a fake customer costume. Bold theory. The manager found a receipt from a different store chain stapled inside the box, so this location couldn't process it. She asked why I hadn't said that. I held up the loyalty app on my phone, showing my actual order from twenty minutes earlier. She left muttering about bad service; the associate picked my blender. Which costume was supposed to say customer?",
      "editor_note": "Rewritten to 138 words with a two-word question hook, every shot phrase preserved, one dry aside, and a costume-specific kicker."
    },
    {
      "slug": "three-year-old-laptop",
      "script": "How old was “new”? My laptop's fan started screaming three months after I bought it. The rep looked up my serial number and said the warranty had expired two years ago because the laptop was manufactured in 2022. I had bought it three weeks earlier, brand new, sealed in plastic, from their own store. He called the manufacturing date final and hung up. Lovely warranty. I called back with the receipt, the store's barcode scan timestamp, and the unboxing video I filmed for a tech channel—all tied to that serial number. A supervisor pulled the manufacturing batch records: a warehouse clerk had mislabeled an entire pallet of unsold 2022 stock, so hundreds bought three year old laptops as current. One call triggered a recall, two years of extended warranty, and my new fan assembly. How “new” was that 2022 pallet?",
      "editor_note": "Rewritten to 140 words with a four-word question hook, every protected number and shot phrase preserved, and a 2022-pallet kicker."
    }
